+### Client descriptor and deadline boundary
+
+The client starts one absolute deadline before descriptor processing and reuses its remaining budget for connect/send/receive. It opens the final descriptor and directory components without following symlinks, pins the directory fd, checks its owner/mode 0700, and verifies the opened descriptor is a current-user-owned regular file mode 0600. Nonblocking open rejects FIFOs/nonregular inputs without waiting for a writer; the read is capped at 4097 bytes to reject more than 4096, with size/timestamp checks for detectable concurrent modification. Symlink substitution at descriptor open fails closed. A path replacement after open cannot redirect that fd. Like the protocol itself, this is not a sandbox against a hostile same-UID process. Regular-file filesystem syscalls are not made cancellable by Python `O_NONBLOCK`: pathological filesystem/kernel stalls may overrun wall-clock time; elapsed budget is checked before/after processing and before any socket operation, and no late descriptor result is admitted.
